## 3. Accurate Calculations

Use consistent assumptions:

- Annual salary = Hourly wage × Hours per week × 52.
- Hourly wage = Annual salary / (Hours per week × 52).
- Weekly wage = Annual salary / 52.
- Biweekly wage = Annual salary / 26.
- Monthly wage = Annual salary / 12.
- Daily wage = Weekly wage / 5, assuming five working days per week.

Requirements:
- Explain the 52-week and five-day assumptions.
- Validate positive weekly hours and nonnegative wages.
- Handle zero salary and invalid inputs.
- Prevent division by zero, NaN and Infinity.
- Preserve full precision and round only for display.
- Do not add unsupported taxes, overtime or payroll deductions.

